<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 22 March, from 871 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vikings" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vikings.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">871 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vikings defeat King Æthelred I of Wessex at Meretun</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> defeated the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> army of King Æthelred I and his brother, the future King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a>, at Meretun, an unknown site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>. Æthelred died after Easter that year and was succeeded by Alfred.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-i-of-wessex">Æthelred I of Wessex</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-heathen-army">Great Heathen Army</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1312">1312 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">714 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Clement V suppresses the Knights Templar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-france">Philip IV of France</a>, Clement V issued the bull Vox in excelso at the Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> abolishing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a>. Their property passed largely to the Hospitallers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1621">1621 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">405 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Plymouth Colony makes a treaty with Massasoit of the Wampanoag</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The settlers of Plymouth Colony under Governor John Carver made a treaty of mutual defence with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massasoit">Massasoit</a>, sachem of the Wampanoag, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisquantum">Tisquantum</a> interpreting. Massasoit kept the peace with the English until his death around 1661.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massasoit">Massasoit</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisquantum">Tisquantum</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1622">1622 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">404 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Powhatan attack kills 347 Virginia colonists</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Warriors under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opechancanough">Opechancanough</a> struck English settlements along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-river">James River</a>, killing about a quarter of the colony's population. The English responded with years of retaliatory war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1765">1765 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">261 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parliament passes the Stamp Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The act taxed printed papers in the American colonies, from newspapers to playing cards. Colonists protested 'no taxation without representation', and Parliament repealed it the next year.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Enslaved insurgents win the Battle of Croix-des-Bouquets</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Enslaved Black insurgents won a victory at Croix-des-Bouquets in the first major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution">Haitian Revolution</a>, their uprising against French colonial rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haitian-revolution">Haitian Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1820">1820 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen Decatur killed in a duel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The naval hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> Wars was mortally wounded by Commodore James Barron at Bladensburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>. His death strengthened public feeling against duelling.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1895">1895 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">131 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lumière brothers show their first film</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, Louis and Auguste Lumière projected 'Workers Leaving the Lumière Factory' with their Cinématographe. Their first paying public screening followed in December.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arab League founded in Cairo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, Transjordan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a>, Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> signed the pact founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-league">League of Arab States</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> joining soon after. It now has 22 members.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lebanon">Lebanon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-i-duke-of-aquitaine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-i-duke-of-aquitaine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William I, Duke of Aquitaine</span><span class="tp">875–918</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maximilian I, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1459–1519</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/august-hermann-francke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/august-hermann-francke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">August Hermann Francke</span><span class="tp">1663–1727</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-doumer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-doumer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul Doumer</span><span class="tp">1857–1932</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emilio-aguinaldo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emilio Aguinaldo</span><span class="tp">1869–1964</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cheddi-jagan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cheddi-jagan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cheddi Jagan</span><span class="tp">1918–1997</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-of-podebrady.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George of Poděbrady</span><span class="tp">1420–1471</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stephen-decatur"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stephen-decatur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stephen Decatur</span><span class="tp">1779–1820</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-wolfgang-von-goethe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johann Wolfgang von Goethe</span><span class="tp">1749–1832</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/song-jiaoren"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/song-jiaoren.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Song Jiaoren</span><span class="tp">1882–1913</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/d-s-senanayake"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/d-s-senanayake.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">D. S. Senanayake</span><span class="tp">1883–1952</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ivan-subasic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivan-subasic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ivan Šubašić</span><span class="tp">1892–1955</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
